        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place the grated courgette in the colander and sprinkle with a little salt. Leave for 5 minutes, then squeeze firmly with both hands to remove as much liquid as possible."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In a bowl, stir together the yoghurt, garlic, olive oil, mint, lemon juice and black pepper until smooth. Season with salt to taste."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fold the squeezed courgette through the yoghurt mixture. Taste and adjust salt and lemon."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Spoon into a serving bowl, drizzle over a little extra olive oil and scatter with a few mint leaves. Serve immediately or refrigerate for up to 2 hours."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Cacik is too watery"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The most common cause is not squeezing enough moisture from the courgette. Salt it, leave it to draw out liquid for 5 minutes, then really wring it out in your fists before adding to the yoghurt."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Too garlicky"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Raw garlic sharpens further as the cacik sits. If making ahead, reduce to 1 clove or stir it in just before serving. Crushing very finely rather than grating also helps distribute it more evenly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Tastes bland"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Salt is doing most of the flavour work here. Season the yoghurt generously, then taste again after adding the courgette, as it dilutes the seasoning. A little extra lemon also helps."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Known across Turkey simply as "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "cacik-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "cacik"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", this yoghurt dip is as fundamental to a Turkish meze spread as bread itself. It cools the palate alongside spiced meats and chilli-spiked dishes, and works equally well as a dip with flatbreads or crudites. The version here uses courgette in place of cucumber, which gives a slightly softer texture. It keeps well in the fridge for a day, though the garlic intensifies overnight."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}